From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:44:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: add gated native object/mesh execution

Folded in:
- drm/asahi: fix mesh command translation borrow and cover admission timeout
- drm/asahi: avoid mesh preparation work when the experiment is disabled
- drm/asahi: wait out native mesh admission during file close
- drm/asahi: use the initialized pool without extra native admission
- drm/asahi: initialize native support mode before first use

[drm/asahi: use the initialized pool without extra native admission]
The required-settings R3 arm passes eight H1 draws with operand aliases and extra admission disabled. Keep the owned, prepopulated 24-buffer pool and remove the unused request/reply lifecycle, deadline polling and close-time wait. Low-priority research settings remain unqualified individually.

[drm/asahi: initialize native support mode before first use]
Set the native support fields while a leased support page is still private, before any render root publication. Preserve all pool identities, pointers and 24-buffer counts. This behavior is gated by native_mesh=1; ordinary support bytes stay identical to #214.
